@@ -150,6 +150,48 @@ and 31.4 with Ornith's and 22.6, 24.6 and 28.6 with Gemma 4's, of its 31.8. Tiel
 with the engine of 1212621baadf, took it to 21.8, 24.9 and 29.9 GiB. Setup does not stop a PC below the 32 GB that
 Qwen3.8 needs when one of these families is named.
 
+## KVMem retained owners
+
+This fork's opt-in KVMem integration can retain an exact native prefix for a
+different conversation without consuming its source. `kvmem.conversation_id`
+selects a mutable lineage; `prompt_cache_key` and `promptCacheKey` are aliases.
+Full UTF-8 keys are bounded at 256 bytes and conflicting aliases are rejected.
+No key is required for a new user Query to discover a compatible prefix. Tool
+continuation uses append and resident-only Pressure, without foreign discovery.
+
+Only sealed host/SSD KV and immutable recurrent checkpoint bytes share physical
+allocations. Each branch has its own accepted identity, checkpoint catalog,
+MeanK, selector, Query, graph feedback and mutable engine state. A failed child
+restore preserves the source. Admission uses the global physical payload
+account plus new growth, not the sum of logical bytes across all owners.
+The native `KVMEM_SHARED` counters expose those scopes separately from RSS.
+Request completion diagnostics report planned/actual cached tokens and the
+native source (`own`, `shared`, `miss`); older engines leave these fields absent.
+Solo MTP and ordinary batch decode retain their existing execution modes.
+Owners also survive solo/batch admission, yielded prefill and MTP continuation;
+continuation after decode has an empty Query span without dropping the owner.
+Prefill yielded before its new Query keeps that still-pending bounded span.
+Foreign discovery requires `--kvmem-sessions` greater than one. With one retained
+history, a different named owner starts fresh instead of taking the active
+owner's mutable lineage. Anonymous single-history behavior stays native.
+
+`CACHE_REUSE` reports the first successful native prefix-restore boundary of an
+HTTP request. Subsequent internal legs cannot inflate this value with input
+already computed by that request. It is not a measure of net compute avoided
+across all later replay. Legacy `DONE` timing fields keep their original scope.
+`KVMEM_SHARED scope_version=2` includes all native sequence archives and slot
+checkpoint references, in addition to parked histories, at request boundaries.
+Logical state references deduplicate their immutable root when reporting
+physical state bytes. The RAM/SSD payload charge includes reservations and can
+overlap cold checkpoint bytes; do not sum these counters into RSS or VRAM.
+`KVMEM_REUSE` traces the effective bounded Query, separately from the requested
+span; a long requested user span is not the amount captured for retrieval.
+Monitor own/shared/miss counters count first native observations once per HTTP
+request and reset with the worker generation. Batch-mode parked/eviction counts
+come from the global native catalog when scope version 2 is available; older
+batch workers keep unsupported fields absent.
+CUDA execution and portable CPU tests are qualified separately from HIP.
+
 ## Elastic experts (opt-in, CUDA)
 
 `strata-poly --elastic-experts` lends audited prompt scratch and expert staging pages to the expert cache
